# predictions.bug

> Module: predictions (Tahmin Motoru) | Category: ANALYTICS  
> Last UI Tested: 02 June 2026

---

### B-PRED-01: "Yeniden Hesapla" (Recalculate) Button Missing

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Severity** | P2 — Medium |
| **Status** | ⬜ **OPEN** |
| **Found** | UI testing — Navigated to `/dashboard/predictions`, page renders, chart visible, but no recalculate button |
| **Bug** | The `predictions.func` specification says there should be a "Yeniden Hesapla" button to trigger `POST /api/tenant/predictions/recalculate`. The body text contains "Tahmin" but there is no clickable recalculate button or any button with text matching "Hesapla", "Yeniden", or "Recalculate". The 12-month chart renders but users cannot trigger a fresh prediction calculation from existing data. |
| **Impact** | Users see stale prediction data and have no way to recompute. If historical data changes (new trips revenue, new expenses), predictions don't update until backend auto-refresh (if any). |
| **Required Fix** | Add a button (e.g., "Yeniden Hesapla") that calls `POST /api/tenant/predictions/recalculate` and reloads the chart data. |
| **Files to Change** | `frontend/src/pages/PredictionsPage.tsx` |
| **CI Gate** | `landing-checks` or new `ui-integrity`: verify PredictionsPage has button with text matching "Hesapla\|Recalculate" |

### B-PRED-02: Predictions Page Shows Chart Without Action

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Severity** | P3 — Low |
| **Status** | ⬜ **OPEN** |
| **Found** | UI testing — page renders chart and table, but no user actions available |
| **Bug** | The predictions page renders a passive view (chart + monthly table) with no interactive elements. Users can view forecasts but cannot trigger recalculation, change date range, filter by category, or export. |
| **Impact** | Module feels incomplete to users — static view without interaction. |
| **Required Fix** | Add at minimum: recalculate button. Optional: date range selector, export to CSV/PDF. |
| **CI Gate** | Same as B-PRED-01 |
